libusb 1.0.27 — for the OpenRSP driver inside the Android apps
==============================================================

Source:   https://github.com/libusb/libusb/releases/download/v1.0.27/libusb-1.0.27.tar.bz2
SHA-256:  ffaa41d741a8a3bee244ac8e54a72ea05bf2879663c098c82fc5757853441575 (verified on download; the same
          hash vendor/openrsp/src/platform/android/Android.cmake pins as SDRPLAY_ANDROID_LIBUSB_SHA256)
Licence:  GNU LGPL 2.1 or later (COPYING).
Contents: COPYING, AUTHORS, README and the libusb/ directory, UNMODIFIED. SHA256SUMS lists every file, and
          android/openrsp/build-openrsp-android.sh refuses to build if any of them differs.

★★ WHY IT IS IN THE TREE. OpenRSP's Android build downloads this tarball at CONFIGURE time unless
   SDRPLAY_ANDROID_LIBUSB_SRC names an extracted tree. A build that reaches the network is a build that breaks
   offline and can change under us, so it is pointed here instead. OpenRSP compiles it STATICALLY with hidden
   visibility into libsdrplay_api.so, so it never meets the libusb1.0.so the other radios use (1.0.26, sdr-kit).
